# BEKW-CODE // GERALD: REFORGE CLASS
## Landfill Recovery Refinery Attachment

**Status:** Conceptual engineering — process architecture and feedstock/output mapping defined, unit-operation BOM pending
**Canon tie-ins:** GERALD (Gyre Class ocean remediation, fate-branches Reef/Island/Ship/Roam), Azrael Alabama Red Dirt Foundry (parallel closed-loop metal refining precedent — laterite feedstock → Alabama Tamahagane), FORGE SYSTEM / Wall Platform / Floor Forge / THE 17 WALLS (the entire downstream materials catalog this refinery exists to feed)
**Design thesis:** The landfill isn't waste. It's an unmined ore body of exactly the materials FORGE, the Wall Platform, and Floor Forge already need — steel, aluminum, polymer, glass, and insulation feedstock, sitting there instead of being dug or drilled for. GERALD: REFORGE closes the loop: landfill in, FORGE-compatible raw material out.

---

## 0. The Core Loop

**MINE (landfill) → SORT → REFINE → CAST/EXTRUDE/COMPOUND → FORGE-COMPATIBLE FEEDSTOCK → downstream FORGE/Wall Platform/Floor Forge manufacturing**

This is the same structural move as Azrael turning depleted-uranium/laterite waste into monument glass and Tamahagane steel, applied at landfill scale instead of contamination-site scale: don't just remediate the waste, extract the exact material streams the rest of the canon is already built to consume.

---

## 1. GERALD: REFORGE as a Fate-Branch

Sits alongside GERALD's existing Reef/Island/Ship/Roam modes as a fifth deployment configuration, but land-based rather than gyre-based:

- **Roam-adjacent mobility** — GERALD's existing autonomous roaming chassis and manipulator systems carry over directly; a landfill is a stationary, bounded, navigable site in the same way an ocean gyre patch is, just on solid ground with different terrain-mobility requirements (tracked/wheeled rather than surface-float)
- **Fixed-installation option** — for landfills large or active enough to warrant it, REFORGE can also deploy as a stationary refinery plant with GERALD units functioning as the mobile mining/sorting front-end feeding a central fixed processing core, rather than each unit carrying full refinery capability itself

---

## 2. Feedstock Sort Streams

Landfill material sorts into five processing streams, each feeding a different part of the FORGE/Wall Platform materials catalog:

### 2.1 Ferrous & Structural Metal
- **Source:** rebar, appliance steel, automotive scrap, structural metal debris
- **Process:** magnetic separation → shredding → melt/refine (same furnace logic as the Azrael foundry, scaled/adapted for mixed scrap rather than laterite ore)
- **Output:** FORGE chassis structural steel stock (SUNFORGE/AMBIENTFORGE core material), Wall Platform structural receiver rail stock, POWERWALL/UTILITYWALL structural framing

### 2.2 Non-Ferrous Metal
- **Source:** aluminum cans/siding/extrusions, copper wiring, brass fittings
- **Process:** eddy-current separation (non-ferrous metals don't respond to magnetic separation, so this needs its own dedicated sort stage) → melt/refine per-alloy
- **Output:** aluminum for lightweight FORGE-4/6 members and Wall Platform receiver rails; copper for Channel A power/data bus wiring across every FORGE-mounted wall and floor class

### 2.3 Polymer / Plastic
- **Source:** HDPE, PP, PVC, mixed film plastics — the actual bulk mass problem in most landfills
- **Process:** sort by resin type (density separation + optical sorting) → wash → shred → compound into engineered composite stock
- **Output:** SUNFORGE/AMBIENTFORGE skin panel composite backing, GREENHOUSEWALL/SUNWALL translucent-core candidate feedstock where resin quality supports it, BATHROOMWALL/BATHWALL nonporous finish panels, general Wall Platform gasket-adjacent elastomer stock where the plastic stream includes rubber/elastomer waste

### 2.4 Glass & Mineral
- **Source:** waste glass, ceramic, concrete rubble, mineral debris
- **Process:** crush → sort by color/composition → melt (glass) or grind (mineral aggregate)
- **Output:** GREENHOUSEWALL glazing stock where glass quality supports it, mineral-fiber insulation core feedstock for FREEZERWALL/THERMALWALL, aggregate filler for structural composite panels

### 2.5 Organic / Unrecoverable
- **Source:** everything that isn't cleanly recoverable as a material stream — the fraction every landfill-recovery system has to be honest about
- **Process:** where feasible, routed to controlled composting or waste-to-energy rather than re-landfilled; this stream should never be inflated by counting it as "recovered" when it isn't
- **Output:** compost feedstock for GROWINGWALL/GREENHOUSEWALL growing-media applications where contamination testing clears it; supplemental process heat if waste-to-energy is used, on the same honest "supplemental, not primary" framing as THERMWEAVE

